### 3.9.5 Keep Alive Timeout Cleanup

If a controller detects a **Keep Alive Timeout**, it shall perform the following actions within the time specified by the **CQT** field (refer to Figure 328):

- Record an **Error Information Log Entry** with status code **Keep Alive Timeout Expired**;
- Stop processing commands;
- Set the **Controller Fatal Status (CSTS.CFS)** bit to **'1'**;
- For **message-based transports**:
  - Terminate the **NVMe Transport connections** for this association;
  - Break the **host-to-controller association**.

After completing these steps, a controller may accept a **Connect command** (refer to section 6.3) for the Admin Queue from the same or another host to form a new association.

If a host detects a **Keep Alive Timeout** and has **outstanding commands without completions** (refer to section 3.4.5), it is **strongly recommended** that the host take steps described in **section 9.6** to avoid possible data corruption from interactions between outstanding and subsequent commands.

### 8.1.1.9 Asymmetric_Namespace_Access_Change_Notifications

If Asymmetric Namespace Access Change Notices are enabled, controllers must send a notification as defined in section 5.2.26.1.5 when:
- The ANA Group Identifier changes (refer to Figure 328);
- An asymmetric namespace access state transition fails (e.g., transition starts but does not complete, returning to the prior state);
- The controller enters any of the following ANA states (excluding state entries due to namespace attachment):
  - ANA Optimized State;
  - ANA Non-Optimized State;
  - ANA Inaccessible State;
  - ANA Persistent Loss State.

### 8.1.8.2 Extended Device Self-Test Operation

- **Completion Time**: Should complete within the time specified in the **Extended Device Self-test Time** field of the *Identify Controller* data structure.
- **Progress Indication**: Percentage complete is reported in the **Current Percentage Complete** field of the *Device Self-test log page* (Section 5.2.12.1.7).
- **Persistence**: The operation persists across **Controller Level Reset** and resumes after power restoration or reset.
  - Resumption occurs at the last segment tested; implementations should retest only from that point.
- **Abortion Conditions**:
  - a) Aborted by a **Format NVM command** (see Figure 644);
  - b) Aborted when a **sanitize operation** starts (Section 5.2.22);
  - c) Aborted if a **Device Self-test command** with **Self-Test Code = Fh** is processed;
  - d) May be aborted if the specified **namespace is removed from the namespace inventory**.
